  "notes_sha256": "a2b25983ba61026ee5a21a4389e3b6e2009e6d2c42a5183bbfced8730f34cdfa",
  "testflight_summary": "- Texture upscaling now works in the Mac app. After an import, you'll see the upscaling progress bar, a \"ready to start\" mark, and Start playing once the main menu's textures are made.\n- The import progress bar now moves from the start of setup, and the percentage never goes backward. Start playing keeps its place on screen and stays disabled until it's ready.\n- Start playing is now a full-size button on Mac (Catalyst), and Return or Enter presses it once it's offered.\n- If storage is too low or the device is too warm, the import screen now says so and VISR tries again later, instead of sitting at 0%. If the import stalls for a minute, Start playing is offered anyway.\n- The in-game settings hub has a new framed layout with a picture and description for each row, plus new VIDEO, AUDIO, and INTERNET artwork.\n- Server browser and menus: scroll arrows show when rows are hidden, long names end in an ellipsis, and the Region column is clearer. The legend uses the game's button art.\n- Vision Pro: use the Enter VR button below the window to play in VR. The Digital Crown exits VR, and holding View and Menu on a controller switches either way.\n- Fixed: the Mac apps now quit on SIGTERM, SIGINT, and SIGHUP. The \"Hold BACK for score\" message no longer shows over the pause menu. Decals no longer flicker at a distance, as on Blood Gulch's base emblems.\n\niCloud Saves is new and starts off. To try it, sign in to iCloud on each device, then turn on iCloud Saves under Network Setup in the game's profile settings (on iPhone, iPad and Apple Vision Pro also on VISR's page in the Settings app). It takes effect at the next launch.\n\nVISR automatically sends missing shader descriptions and device model information to improve loading. Reports exclude gameplay and personal file names. Apple's upload service attaches an account-specific identifier. Shader diagnostics are required in builds with shader uploads enabled.\n\nVISR automatically sends game performance data to improve the game. Reports exclude names, chat, and personal file names. Apple's upload service attaches an account-specific identifier. Performance diagnostics are required in builds with performance reports enabled. Sharing this data is part of testing; leaving the beta stops it.",
  "testflight_summary_sha256": "fd96241d7686a0f90786706a030c0b36c03d095880a53299b8a76a0587fc6492",
